n that you really wanted but you  didn't get it and at those times it may  feel tempting to forfeit to give up but  it is up to you to make most of that  situation so when you face that  situation I'd love for you to remember  words of John Wooden probably the most  famous coach in the history of college  sports who said when things go bad for  reasons we don't control it is very  tempting to first blame and then embrace  fate as a reason for our failure but  this is not what effective leaders do  okay so my last story is about getting  support team so let's now I'll go back  to Wimbledon you're playing that final  so you're ready like on the central card  you're warming up and as you're warming  up you glanced over to your box and you  see your coach there your trainer you're  hitting partner I love with your friends  and family and you realize how lucky you  are you are here because you've worked  really hard but you're also here because  of their hard work and their support now  is this really that much different from  business I'll argue no our ability to  succeed in a business place will depend  on our hard work but also in the  strength of our support team yes for  some reason  when we talk about coaching in athletics  it's normal and obvious but it gets a  little uncomfortable when we talk about  it in the worlds of business I remember  a few months ago a CEO of a fortune 500  company came to our class and he talked  about working with coaches and  counselors when we were reflected back  on his presentation you know some of us  express admiration for him sharing the  story but some people were outwardly and  easy I remember one person saying you  know if I knew that my coach was seeing  a counselor or my boss was seeing a  coach or counselor I'm not sure if I  wanted to work for him if I would have  faith for him and that was so  interesting to me because in sports  exactly opposite it's not only normal it  was actually crucial to your success  that see how I ended his talk by saying  if you could get help why wouldn't you  if you could become a better leader why  wouldn't you why wouldn't you today I  have talked to you about parallels  between world of sports and worlds of  business I've told you how tennis  players go about winning their game and  if I were to summarize my whole talk in  just one word it would be ownership on  your preparation on your response and  all your support system I hope some of  these lessons resonated with you and  will help you win your own game
 

